      "side": 1,
      "message": "**1. Defining Kconfigs via Compiler Flags**\nIn `CMakeLists.txt`:\n\n```cmake\ntarget_compile_definitions(app PRIVATE\n    CONFIG_HAVE_FT_LOCKER_PRIVATE_ALGORITHM\u003d1\n)\n\n```\n\n* **Issue:** Defining `CONFIG_*` variables directly through `-D` compiler flags bypasses Kconfig. This breaks Zephyr tooling (like `guiconfig` or Kconfig dependency trees) and violates the rule that `CONFIG_` macros are strictly generated by the Kconfig system in `autoconf.h`.\n* **Suggestion:** Move this to `prj.conf` as `CONFIG_HAVE_FT_LOCKER_PRIVATE_ALGORITHM\u003dy` (and ensure a corresponding Kconfig entry exists). If this macro is purely a test-suite mock flag and doesn\u0027t exist in Kconfig, remove the `CONFIG_` prefix entirely (e.g., just `HAVE_FT_LOCKER_PRIVATE_ALGORITHM\u003d1`) to avoid confusing maintainers.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "d3f21f0a98d57f63bb35c4046000eea813f4fbc8",
