      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T16:19:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**1. Uninitialized Buffer Passed to System Under Test**\nIn the fixture, `fake_image` is defined but never initialized:\n\n```c\nstruct ft98xx_bio_alg_fixture {\n\tconst struct fingerprint_algorithm *alg;\n\tuint8_t fake_image[FT_RAW_SIZE + 100];\n};\n\n```\n\n* **Issue:** You pass `fixture-\u003efake_image` into `fingerprint_enroll_step` and `fingerprint_match` in several tests. Because it is uninitialized memory (beyond any implicit zeroing during the one-time static setup), if the `ft98xx_bio_alg.c` driver contains any code that reads headers/metadata from this image *before* passing it to the mocked `focal_algo_*` functions, the test will branch non-deterministically. Furthermore, if you run this test suite under Clang Memory Sanitizer (MSAN) or Valgrind, it will trigger \"use of uninitialized value\" errors.\n* **Suggestion:** Initialize the buffer explicitly in `ft98xx_alg_before`:\n\n```c\nmemset(fixture-\u003efake_image, 0, sizeof(fixture-\u003efake_image));\n\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 43,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 43,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "d3f21f0a98d57f63bb35c4046000eea813f4fbc8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
