      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T16:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**1. Relying on Transitive Includes for Standard Macros**\nThe tests utilize system macros like `-EINVAL` and `BIT(0)`:\n\n```c\nzassert_equal(fingerprint_algorithm_init(fixture-\u003ealg), -EINVAL);\n// ...\nzassert_equal(update_bitmap, BIT(0));\n\n```\n\n* **Issue:** Neither `\u003cerrno.h\u003e` (for `EINVAL`) nor `\u003czephyr/sys/util.h\u003e` (for `BIT`) are explicitly included in `ft98xx.c`. The code compiles only because these headers happen to be pulled in transitively by `\u003czephyr/ztest.h\u003e`. If the Zephyr project refactors the includes in the ZTEST subsystem in a future release, this test file will suddenly fail to compile.\n* **Suggestion:** Always explicitly include the headers for the macros you use:\n\n```c\n#include \u003cerrno.h\u003e\n#include \u003czephyr/sys/util.h\u003e\n\n```",
      "range": {
