      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T16:10:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**1. Uninitialized Output Parameters in Custom Mock**\nIn `custom_get_finger_detailed_info_too_large`, you assign a value to `*finger_size` but fail to assign values to `*subtpl_size` and `*head_size`.\n\n```c\nstatic int custom_get_finger_detailed_info_too_large(int *finger_size,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t     int *subtpl_size,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t     int *head_size)\n{\n\tif (finger_size)\n\t\t*finger_size \u003d CONFIG_FP_ALGORITHM_TEMPLATE_SIZE + 1;\n\t// Missing subtpl_size and head_size assignments\n\treturn 0;\n}\n\n```\n\n* **Issue:** When the SUT (System Under Test) calls this function, it likely passes pointers to uninitialized local variables. If it subsequently reads `subtpl_size` or `head_size` to calculate the total required buffer size, it will read garbage memory. This can lead to undefined behavior or flaky test failures depending on what happens to be on the stack.\n* **Suggestion:** Ensure all requested output parameters are populated with safe defaults.\n\n```c\n\tif (subtpl_size) *subtpl_size \u003d 0;\n\tif (head_size) *head_size \u003d 0;\n\n```",
