      "side": 1,
      "message": "**2. Testing `exit` out of order in `test_exit_success**`\n\n```c\nZTEST_F(ft98xx_bio_alg, test_exit_success)\n{\n\tzassert_ok(fingerprint_algorithm_exit(fixture-\u003ealg));\n\tzassert_equal(focal_algo_deinit_fake.call_count, 1);\n}\n\n```\n\n* **Issue:** This test calls `exit()` without ever calling `init()`. While it happens to pass here, calling teardown APIs on uninitialized drivers is an unrealistic lifecycle and often triggers null-pointer dereferences or crashes in real implementations.\n* **Suggestion:** Call `fingerprint_algorithm_init(fixture-\u003ealg);` right before the exit call in this test.",
