      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T16:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**3. Implicitly Unmocked Return Values**\nIn several tests, you call APIs that execute sub-routines (e.g., `fingerprint_enroll_start` calling `focal_algo_enroll_start`), but you don\u0027t explicitly set the mock\u0027s return value.\n\n* **Issue:** FFF zero-initializes mock return values upon `RESET_FAKE`, so `focal_algo_enroll_start_fake.return_val` defaults to `0` (Success). While this works, it makes the test logic implicit.\n* **Suggestion:** For readability and strictness, explicitly set the success returns for the mocks in the `ft98xx_alg_before` setup block just like you did for `focal_algo_init_fake.return_val \u003d 0;`. Include `focal_algo_enroll_start_fake`, `focal_algo_match_fake`, etc.",
