      "side": 1,
      "message": "**1. Magic Numbers vs Constants in Math**\nIn `test_enroll_step_success_and_progress`:\n\n```c\nzassert_equal(completion, (1 * 100) / total_samples,\n\t      \"Completion should be ~8%% after 1 step.\");\n\n```\n\n* **Suggestion:** You nicely parameterized `total_samples \u003d SINGLE_FINGER_ENROLL_NUM;`, but hardcoded `12` in your brain to write `~8%%` in the string. If `SINGLE_FINGER_ENROLL_NUM` changes in the driver header, the math still works, but the log message becomes a lie. Keep the string generic (e.g., `\"Completion should correctly reflect 1 out of N steps\"`).",
