      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T16:22:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**1. Unverified Anti-Spoofing Flag (Bypassing Hardware)**\nIn `test_match_success_no_update`, you call `fingerprint_match` with what appears to be a `false` flag for anti-spoofing:\n\n```c\n\tint res \u003d fingerprint_match(fixture-\u003ealg, template_buf, 1,\n\t\t\t\t    fixture-\u003efake_image, false, \u0026match_index,\n\t\t\t\t    \u0026update_bitmap);\n\n```\n\nHowever, you explicitly set up the anti-spoofing mock (`focal_algo_anti_spoofing_fake.return_val \u003d 0;`) but never check its call count.\n\n* **Issue:** The point of passing `false` to the match API is likely to instruct the algorithm to skip a costly hardware anti-spoofing check. If the driver contains a bug where it executes the spoofing check anyway, this test will pass silently, missing the bug.\n* **Suggestion:** Add an assertion to strictly verify that the driver respected the flag and skipped the hardware call:\n\n```c\nzassert_equal(focal_algo_anti_spoofing_fake.call_count, 0, \n              \"Spoofing check must be skipped when flag is false\");\n\n```",
